00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in this video you will learn how to  enable and connect to the serial console  for google compute engine or gc virtual  machine instances running on linux  operating system  to begin with let's understand what a  serial console is  serial console allows users to access  virtual machine instances through a  virtual serial connection  typically in linux systems the first  serial port is used as the serial  console  you may be wondering why do i need a  serial console  when an instance is inaccessible over a  network for example when ssh fails or  the vm is partially booted you can  access the instance by using its serial  console  thereby enables you to troubleshoot  boot networking issues and also interact  with the bootloader  by default the serial console is  disabled to restrict access and google  recommends that you use it only for  troubleshooting purposes  to use serial console you must enable it  either at the project level for all  instances or at an instance level for a  specific instance  remember if there is an instance level  setting present then it overrides any  project level setting  before enabling the access to the serial  console remember that access to the  serial console can be disabled by  setting an organization policy which  disables interactive serial console  access to all vms for all the projects  that are part of the organization  you can turn off the enforcement of the  organization level policy on a per  project basis by following the steps in  this documentation  now let's jump into the google cloud  console and learn how to enable access  to the serial console at an instance  level  go to compute engine vm instances page  click on the instance you want to enable  access for  in our example we will select my  instance which is currently inaccessible  over the network  click edit  in the remote access section  check enable connecting to the serial  ports box and save your changes  now we can connect to the serial console  using google cloud console the google  cloud cli or third-party ssh client  provided that ssh client lets you to  connect to the tcp port  9600  in our demo we will access the  problematic instance  my instance through the serial console  by using google cloud console  select my instance  in the remote access section  click connect to the serial console to  connect to default port  port 1.  as we see in the serial console  the instance is in emergency mode  and is not booting up thereby making it  inaccessible through ssh congratulations  we have successfully used the serial  console to determine the cause of vm  inaccessibility  now let's look at another scenario when  a vm is booted but isn't accessible over  the network you must enter your login  credential through the serial console  by default google supplied linux system  images are not configured to allow  password-based logins for local users  one of the ways to overcome this  limitation is to set up a local password  by using a startup script  to configure a startup script that sets  a local user assigns that user a  password and gives them a permission to  operate as root  we will do the following  in the cloud console go to vm instances  page  select the vm for which you want to add  the local password  click edit  in  startup script section enter the  following script  you can find the script in our  documentation shared in the description  below click save  reset the vm to initialize startup  script  then connect to serial console  enter your login information  congratulations we have now successfully  logged into the vm instance through the  serial console even though the instance  was not accessible through ssh  thereby enabling us to troubleshoot  further at the operating system level  check out this documentation for further  tips and tricks you can use while  connecting to the gc instances through  the serial console  [Music]  you

